course: dictionary
lesson: 3723
title: Old words and names with capitals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are old-fashioned, so you will rarely hear them today. You can still work them out from the words around them. «The old wreck was smashed to flinders by the storm.» The storm did the smashing, and a wreck is a broken ship, so flinders must mean broken bits.
explain: Look for a capital letter too. A capital letter in the middle of a sentence often means a name of a person or a place. «Old Man Kangaroo is chased past the Flinders and the Darling Downs» names a place, because the Flinders and the Darling Downs are both on a map of Australia.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word. If «smashed into small broken pieces» still makes sense, your guess is right.
fact: Flinders means small broken pieces or splinters.
fact: «Smashed to flinders» means smashed into tiny broken bits.
fact: Flinders is an old-fashioned plural noun, so people rarely use it today.
fact: Flinders is also a name: Matthew Flinders was an English navigator who sailed round Australia from 1801 to 1803.
fact: Many places are named after him, such as the Flinders Ranges and Flinders Street in Melbourne.
exercise: What does «smashed to flinders» mean? | Painted bright red | *Smashed into small broken pieces | Pulled up out of the sea | Still whole and shiny
exercise: In «Old Man Kangaroo is chased past the Flinders», what kind of word is Flinders? | *A place name, like a mountain range | A kind of wild desert plant | Something that means small broken pieces | A type of ship's sail
exercise: Matthew Flinders was a navigator. What was his job? | A baker who sold bread | *A sailor who charted the coasts and found the way across the sea | A farmer who grew wheat | A teacher of art
test: Why does Flinders start with a capital letter when it is a name? | *It names a person or a place | It is always the first word in a sentence | It is a plural noun | It is an old word
test: A glass that is «smashed to flinders» is | Still in one piece | Mended with glue | *Broken into tiny bits | Covered in paint
exam: In which sentence is Flinders a proper name? | «Flinders are small splinters of wood.» | «The flinders on the floor glittered in the sun.» | «The storm smashed the boat to flinders.» | *«We drove through the Flinders Ranges on our holiday.»
